cask "git-strata-desktop" do
  version "@VERSION@"

  on_arm do
    sha256 "@DMG_SHA256@"

    url "https://github.com/dickwu/git-strata/releases/download/v#{version}/Git-Strata_#{version}_arm64.dmg"
  end

  name "GIT STRATA"
  desc "Desktop app for git-strata sessions"
  homepage "https://github.com/dickwu/git-strata"

  livecheck do
    url :url
    strategy :github_latest
  end

  auto_updates true
  depends_on arch: :arm64
  depends_on macos: :ventura

  app "GIT STRATA.app"

  uninstall quit: "io.github.dickwu.git-strata"

  # Keep the app's Application Support directory for update and daemon move
  # recovery. Preserve the daemon's config, pins and configured data root.
  zap trash: [
    "~/Library/Caches/io.github.dickwu.git-strata",
    "~/Library/Preferences/io.github.dickwu.git-strata.plist",
    "~/Library/Saved Application State/io.github.dickwu.git-strata.savedState",
    "~/Library/WebKit/io.github.dickwu.git-strata",
  ]

  caveats <<~EOS
    Unless this release is notarized, macOS blocks the first open: allow it in
    System Settings > Privacy & Security > Open Anyway.
    If the app is not listed there, run:
      sudo xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine "/Applications/GIT STRATA.app"

    This app includes the daemon and command-line tools. On a fresh install,
    open GIT STRATA and choose Set up daemon in the Daemon panel.

    Run this before upgrading an existing desktop install whose daemon uses
    the formula. It keeps Homebrew from autoremoving the formula when the cask
    drops the dependency.

      brew tab --installed-on-request dickwu/tap/git-strata

    The 0.3.0 release notes show the order for upgrading the formula and app.
      https://github.com/dickwu/git-strata/blob/main/docs/release-notes/v0.3.0.md

    After moving the daemon into the app, use the in-app updater. Homebrew can
    still replace the app, for example with a greedy upgrade. If it does, follow
    the app's Restart daemon prompt. A daemon crash before that restart can
    cause launchd to start the new bundled binary before you confirm the change.

    Once the LaunchAgent runs the bundled daemon, quit GIT STRATA and stop
    the daemon before uninstalling the app.

      git-strata daemon stop

    Use the app's copy if git-strata is absent from PATH.

      "/Applications/GIT STRATA.app/Contents/MacOS/git-strata" daemon stop

    If the stop times out, leave the files in place and wait for daemon work
    to finish. Resolve any other stop error before continuing. Check the job
    with launchctl print.

      launchctl print gui/$(id -u)/com.gwd.git-stratad

    If the job is still loaded after a timeout, retry the stop and check again.
    Continue only when print explicitly reports that the service could not be
    found in this domain (exit 113). Remove the plist at
    ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.gwd.git-stratad.plist and the git-strata and
    git-stratad symlinks in /opt/homebrew/bin (or /usr/local/bin) that point
    into this app. Then run `brew uninstall --cask dickwu/tap/git-strata-desktop`
    or move the app to the Trash. Keep the config, store and sessions.
  EOS
end
